      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "329736c9-493e-5dde-82d5-de67b32ba0d0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: The Jungle Book (1967 film), The Lone Ranger (2013 film)\n- People: Mowgli, Bagheera, Baloo, Shere Khan, Gore Verbinski, Justin Haythe, Ted Elliott, Terry Rossio, Johnny Depp, Armie Hammer, William Fichtner, Barry Pepper, Ruth Wilson, James Badge Dale, Tom Wilkinson, Helena Bonham Carter, Phil Harris, Joel Harlow\n- Companies: Walt Disney Productions\n- Roles: Tonto, John Reid, the Lone Ranger\n- Topics: animated musical adventure films, western action films, radio adaptations, Academy Award for Best Makeup and Hairstyling\n\nFacts:\n- The Jungle Book is a 1967 American animated musical adventure film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\n- The Jungle Book follows Mowgli, a feral child raised by wolves in the Indian jungle, as Bagheera and Baloo try to persuade him to leave before Shere Khan arrives.\n- Phil Harris played Baloo in The Jungle Book in 1967.\n- Phil Harris played Thomas O'Malley in The Aristocats in 1970.\n- Phil Harris played Little John in Robin Hood in 1973.\n- Joel Harlow won the Academy Award for Best Makeup and Hairstyling in 2009 for his work on Star Trek.\n- The Lone Ranger is a 2013 American western action film directed by Gore Verbinski and written by Justin Haythe, Ted Elliott, and Terry Rossio.\n- The Lone Ranger is based on the radio series of the same name and stars Johnny Depp as Tonto, who narrates the events, and Armie Hammer as John Reid, the Lone Ranger.\n- The Lone Ranger tells Tonto's memories of the duo's earliest attempts to stop local villainy and bring justice to the American Old West.\n- The Lone Ranger features William Fichtner, Barry Pepper, Ruth Wilson, James Badge Dale, Tom Wilkinson, and Helena Bonham Carter in supporting roles.\n- The Lone Ranger was the first theatrical film to feature the Lone Ranger and Tonto characters in more than 32 years.\n- Joel Harlow was nominated again for the Academy Award for Best Makeup and Hairstyling in 2013 for The Lone Ranger.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
