        "text": "Page: The Jungle Book (1967 film). Sentence: The Jungle Book is a 1967 American animated musical adventure film produced by Walt Disney Productions.\nPage: The Jungle Book (1967 film). Sentence: The plot follows Mowgli, a feral child raised in the Indian jungle by wolves, as his friends Bagheera the panther and Baloo the bear try to convince him to leave the jungle before the evil tiger Shere Khan arrives.\nPage: The Lone Ranger (2013 film). Sentence: The Lone Ranger is a 2013 American western action film directed by Gore Verbinski from a screenplay written by Justin Haythe, Ted Elliott and Terry Rossio.\nPage: The Lone Ranger (2013 film). Sentence: Based on the radio series of the same name, the film stars Johnny Depp as Tonto, the narrator of the events, and Armie Hammer as John Reid, the Lone Ranger.\nPage: The Lone Ranger (2013 film). Sentence: It relates Tonto's memories of the duo's earliest efforts to subdue local villainy and bring justice to the American Old West.\nPage: The Lone Ranger (2013 film). Sentence: William Fichtner, Barry Pepper, Ruth Wilson, James Badge Dale, Tom Wilkinson and Helena Bonham Carter also are featured in supporting roles.\nPage: The Lone Ranger (2013 film). Sentence: It is the first theatrical film featuring the Lone Ranger and Tonto characters in more than 32 years.\nPage: Phil Harris. Sentence: He played Baloo the bear in \"The Jungle Book\" (1967), Thomas O'Malley in \"The Aristocats\" (1970), and Little John in \"Robin Hood\" (1973).\nPage: Joel Harlow. Sentence: Harlow won the Academy Award for Best Makeup and Hairstyling in 2009 for his work on \"Star Trek\", and was once again nominated in 2013 for \"The Lone Ranger\".",
